{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,200p' README.md\"","aggregated_output":"/opt/homebrew/Library/Homebrew/cmd/shellenv.sh: line 18: /bin/ps: Operation not permitted\n# HeroKid Monorepo\n\nHeroKid now runs on a pnpm-managed Turborepo so the Expo mobile app, Next.js 15 web app, and shared tooling evolve together. The repo currently targets Node 18+ and pnpm 9.\n\n## Workspace Layout\n\n```\n.\n├── apps\n│   ├── mobile        # Expo Router project (EAS-ready)\n│   └── web           # Next.js 15 app router project\n├── packages\n│   ├── api           # Shared tRPC routers + client helpers\n│   ├── database      # Prisma schema + Supabase migrations\n│   └── shared        # TS config, ESLint, Prettier, Jest config + helpers\n├── turbo.json        # Pipeline definition for dev/build/lint/test\n└── pnpm-workspace.yaml\n```\n\n- pnpm workspaces keep dependency installation fast and deterministic across apps.\n- Turborepo orchestrates shared tasks (`dev`, `build`, `lint`, `test`) with caching.\n\n## Commands\n\n| Command | What it does |\n| --- | --- |\n| `pnpm install` | Installs dependencies for every workspace (pnpm hoists shared deps). |\n| `pnpm dev` | Runs `expo start` and `next dev` concurrently via Turborepo. |\n| `pnpm build` | Executes production builds for web + mobile plus shared package type builds. |\n| `pnpm lint` | Applies the shared ESLint config to all workspaces. |\n| `pnpm test` | Runs Jest (shared package) and Vitest (web) test suites. |\n| `pnpm turbo run db:migrate` | Applies committed Prisma migrations to the Supabase database referenced by `DATABASE_URL`. |\n\n## Environment Bootstrap\n\n1. Copy `.env.example` to `.env.local` (or `.env`) and fill the Supabase secrets from the engineering vault.  \n2. Follow `docs/technical/supabase-runbook.md` when rotating keys—GitHub Actions, Vercel, and EAS secrets share the same names as the template file.  \n3. Run `pnpm install` and then `pnpm --filter @herokid/database db:status` to confirm the Prisma schema can connect to whichever Supabase environment your `DATABASE_URL` points to.\n\n## Supabase Setup\n\n- `supabase/config.toml` mirrors the Supabase CLI defaults so `supabase start` or other CLI commands use our documented ports, schemas, and `.env.local` secrets.  \n- `pnpm supabase:plan` runs the provisioning script in dry-run mode, while `pnpm supabase:apply:dev` / `pnpm supabase:apply:prod` apply the plan for each environment (wrappers over `scripts/bootstrap-supabase.mjs`).  \n- Storage lifecycle automation lives in `scripts/storage-lifecycle.mjs` (tested via `node --test scripts/storage-lifecycle.test.mjs`). Use `pnpm supabase:storage:dev` / `pnpm supabase:storage:prod` for dry-run cleanups before running with destructive flags.  \n- Auth templates + configuration guidance (COPPA consent copy, password policies, signed URLs only) are documented in `docs/technical/supabase-runbook.md`, and the HTML templates live in `supabase/auth/email-templates/`.\n\n## Tech Stack Snapshot\n\n- **Monorepo:** Turborepo 2.x + pnpm 9 workspaces\n- **Mobile:** Expo SDK 51 (Expo Router, EAS profiles included)\n- **Web:** Next.js 15 App Router with Edge-ready `/api/health`\n- **API:** Shared tRPC routers (`packages/api`) backed by Prisma + Supabase\n- **Shared Tooling:** Centralized TS config, ESLint, Prettier, Jest (`packages/shared`)\n- **Testing:** Jest (`packages/shared`) + Vitest/RTL (`apps/web`)\n\n## Contribution Guidelines\n\n1. Use feature branches (e.g., `feature/story-1-1-turborepo-setup`) off of `develop`.\n2. Run `pnpm lint` and `pnpm test` before pushing to keep caches green.\n3. Document new scripts or workspace changes in this README.\n4. Keep shared tooling in `packages/shared` so other workspaces inherit updates automatically.\n5. Prefer workspace filters when iterating locally (e.g., `pnpm --filter @herokid/web dev`).\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- Story 1.2: Wire Supabase provisioning scripts under `packages/database`.\n- Story 1.3: Stand up the typed tRPC API surface and Prisma client (`packages/api`).\n- Story 1.4+: Configure Vercel + CI/CD to deploy the new structure automatically.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
