{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_129","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat <<'EOF' > .claude/skills/orchestration-skill/logs/results/8b284fb8.summary.md\nVERDICT: NOT READY\nHealth Score: 55%\nTop Strengths:\n- Feature surface is comprehensive: auth, child profiles, avatar generation, story engine, credits, PDF export, and cron jobs are all implemented across web/mobile + tRPC (\"'`packages/api/src/routers/*`).\n- Strong guardrails: rate limits, audit logging, ownership checks, and COPPA consent enforcement are present in the API layer (e.g., `packages/api/src/routers/auth.ts`, `avatar.ts`).\n- Payments/webhooks use proper signature verification and ledger updates (Stripe route in `apps/web/app/api/webhooks/stripe/route.ts`).\nTop Concerns/Blockers:\n- AI clients throw at import time when `GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT` is unset; env template omits this, so the server cannot start in a fresh prod env (`packages/ai/src/imagen/client.ts:489-505`, `packages/ai/src/gemini/client.ts:55-60`).\n- Story/Avatar generation relies on Vertex AI + Supabase storage credentials that are not validated or documented in `.env.example`, so core flows (avatars/stories) will fail until keys/service accounts and buckets are provisioned.\n- Test/CI state unknown: 54 test files exist but were not executed in this assessment; migrations were not validated, so runtime regressions or schema drift may exist.\nCritical Issues Before Launch:\n- Add required Google/Vertex env vars (project id + service account creds) to configuration and guard imports so services don’t crash when unset.\n- Verify Supabase buckets/keys for stories, temp uploads, and PDFs are configured; run `prisma migrate status` against the target DB to confirm schema matches code.\n- Run the full lint/test/build pipeline (pnpm lint/test/build) in a production-like env to catch compile/runtime failures, especially across Next 15 RC + React 19 RC.\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
